My healer Mender found a +4 ring of adornment on
DLVL1, and a huge, but not very interesting, 40 item
armor shop on DLVL2.

Credit cloning when the shopkeeper sells you goods
for the same value for which he buys them is much
like shooting fish in a barrel, and at Ch:20, that's
pretty much the way things go. Mender went in with
1200 z, is leaving with 4600 z, during the
bankrupting of the shopkeeper, the only decrease in
credit was for the 75% random price decreases off
and on that went more often in favor of the
shopkeeper than the shoplifter.

4600 z plus speed boots, +2 Leather armor, and an
etched helmet.

Same drill again on DLVL3, this time in a General
store. Left with 8500 z, a puzzled shopkeeper, lots
of unIDed goodies, and both a +0 oilskin cloak
(carried) and a +1 cloak of protection (worn), now
at AC:-2.

Not much luck with newts so far, though, 13 killed,
only one mild buzz, still can't cast healing.

An impoverished shopkeeper on DLVL6 upped the free
gold ante to 9800 z, but two human mummies on bones
level DLVL7 separated the pet large dog Muncher from
healer Mender, and an ill considered zap of Mender's
wand of sleep bounced off an amulet one human mummy,
"john" was wearing, and put Mender to sleep and
rather quickly thereafter under a tombstone.

Sigh.

